cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'Generative AI for Physics Analysis (ePIC tutorial)'
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Alexandr
    family-names: Prozorov
  - name: The ePIC Collaboration
abstract: >-
  A tool-agnostic, hands-on lesson that teaches researchers to use generative
  AI — AI coding assistants, MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool servers, skills,
  and agents — for a real ePIC physics analysis: reconstructing the decay
  Lambda0 -> p pi- and fitting its invariant-mass peak at 1.115683 GeV. Built
  with The Carpentries Workbench.
keywords:
  - generative AI
  - AI assistant
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - EIC
  - ePIC
  - physics analysis
  - uproot
  - EDM4eic
repository-code: 'https://github.com/aprozo/tutorial-mcp'
license: CC-BY-4.0
